      "seed": 1819452767,
      "version": 696,
      "versionNonce": 170057393,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742828520828,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design Leetcode\n\nFunctional requirements:\n\n1. User can view problems based on various filters(difficulty, tags: binarysearch, Hashmap)\n2. User can submit solution to a problem\n3. Multiple language supported\n4. Participate in competitions\n    i. Leaderboard\n    ii. Surges\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\nHigh availability - Submissions, fetching problems, etc. (availability > consistency)\nEventual consistency\nScalability: 5M accounts, 1M DAU\nSecurity and isolation\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n1. Read/write throughput\n    5M users, 1M DAU\n    Reads: 10M reads -> 10M/86400 -> 100 TPS -> 1k TPS\n    writes: 1 : 10 -> 1M writes -> 10 TPS -> 100 TPS\n2. Storage\n    problems -> 3k * 1MB -> 1 GB\n    submission -> 10M * 1KB -> 10GB \n    ~ 15 GB * 2 ~ 30 GB\n    30GB * 365 * 10 ~ 100 TB\n    \n\nCore Entities:\n1. User\n    userId\n    name\n    rating\n    contestParticipated\n    level: RatingLevel (KNIGHT, ...)\n\n2. Problem\n    problemId\n    textDescription\n    textImages: []\n    sampleTestCases\n    constraints\n    createdAt\n\n3. Submission\n    submissionId\n    code\n    language\n    status: SubmissionStatus (PENDING, ACCEPTED, FAILED, STARTED)\n    rejectReason: TLE | MLE | WRONG_ANSWER\n    submittedAt: timestamp\n\n4. Contest\n    contestId\n    problemIds: []\n    startTime: timestamp\n    endTime: timestamp\n    participants: number\n\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. GET /api/v1/problems?filters={tags, difficulty}&page=1&limit=20&sortBy=timestamp\nRequest headers -> JWT token -> userId\n\n{\n    [\n    {\n        \"problemId\": \"\",\n        \"\"\n    }\n    ]\n}\n\nResponse -> Partial[Problem]\n200: success\n400: bad request\n\n2. GET /api/v1/problems/{problemId}\n\nResponse -> Problem\n\n3. POST /api/v1/problems/{problemId}/submission\n{\n    \"contestId\": \"\",\n    \"code\": \"\",\n    \"language\": \"\",\n    \"\"\n}\n\n4. GET /api/v1/problems/{problemId}/submissions/{submissionId}\n\n{\n    \"code\": \"\",\n    \"sumittedAt\": \"\"\n    \"status\": \"ACCEPTED\" | \"REJECTED\" \n}\n\n5. GET /api/v1/contest/{contestId}/leaderboard?page=1&limit=20\n\nResponse ->\n{\n    \"ranking\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"\",\n            \"problemsAccepted\": \"\",\n            \"score\": \"\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design Leetcode\n\nFunctional requirements:\n\n1. User can view problems based on various filters(difficulty, tags: binarysearch, Hashmap)\n2. User can submit solution to a problem\n3. Multiple language supported\n4. Participate in competitions\n    i. Leaderboard\n    ii. Surges\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\nHigh availability - Submissions, fetching problems, etc. (availability > consistency)\nEventual consistency\nScalability: 5M accounts, 1M DAU\nSecurity and isolation\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n1. Read/write throughput\n    5M users, 1M DAU\n    Reads: 10M reads -> 10M/86400 -> 100 TPS -> 1k TPS\n    writes: 1 : 10 -> 1M writes -> 10 TPS -> 100 TPS\n2. Storage\n    problems -> 3k * 1MB -> 1 GB\n    submission -> 10M * 1KB -> 10GB \n    ~ 15 GB * 2 ~ 30 GB\n    30GB * 365 * 10 ~ 100 TB\n    \n\nCore Entities:\n1. User\n    userId\n    name\n    rating\n    contestParticipated\n    level: RatingLevel (KNIGHT, ...)\n\n2. Problem\n    problemId\n    textDescription\n    textImages: []\n    sampleTestCases\n    constraints\n    createdAt\n\n3. Submission\n    submissionId\n    code\n    language\n    status: SubmissionStatus (PENDING, ACCEPTED, FAILED, STARTED)\n    rejectReason: TLE | MLE | WRONG_ANSWER\n    submittedAt: timestamp\n\n4. Contest\n    contestId\n    problemIds: []\n    startTime: timestamp\n    endTime: timestamp\n    participants: number\n\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. GET /api/v1/problems?filters={tags, difficulty}&page=1&limit=20&sortBy=timestamp\nRequest headers -> JWT token -> userId\n\n{\n    [\n    {\n        \"problemId\": \"\",\n        \"\"\n    }\n    ]\n}\n\nResponse -> Partial[Problem]\n200: success\n400: bad request\n\n2. GET /api/v1/problems/{problemId}\n\nResponse -> Problem\n\n3. POST /api/v1/problems/{problemId}/submission\n{\n    \"contestId\": \"\",\n    \"code\": \"\",\n    \"language\": \"\",\n    \"\"\n}\n\n4. GET /api/v1/problems/{problemId}/submissions/{submissionId}\n\n{\n    \"code\": \"\",\n    \"sumittedAt\": \"\"\n    \"status\": \"ACCEPTED\" | \"REJECTED\" \n}\n\n5. GET /api/v1/contest/{contestId}/leaderboard?page=1&limit=20\n\nResponse ->\n{\n    \"ranking\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"\",\n            \"problemsAccepted\": \"\",\n            \"score\": \"\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
